wayland-server: a window whose toplevel is gone ignores activation and resizing

When a client destroys an xdg_toplevel (Wine does whenever it hides a
window), ~HaikuXdgToplevel clears the window's fToplevel and posts
B_QUIT_REQUESTED; QuitRequested() expects the NULL. A B_WINDOW_ACTIVATED or
B_WINDOW_RESIZED already queued for the window is dispatched first, and
WindowActivated()/FrameResized() dereferenced the NULL toplevel: the
window thread crashed (Half-Life full screen, which hides and shows its
launcher's window at every frame: WindowActivated+0x4c, a load at 0x58),
and with it the program.

--- a/HaikuXdgToplevel.cpp
+++ b/HaikuXdgToplevel.cpp
@@ -58,6 +58,9 @@
 void WaylandWindow::WindowActivated(bool isActive)
 {
 	WaylandEnv vlEnv(this);
+	// the toplevel is gone, the B_QUIT_REQUESTED it posted not handled yet
+	if (fToplevel == NULL)
+		return;
 	if (isActive != fToplevel->fState.activated) {
 		fToplevel->fState.activated = !fToplevel->fState.activated;
 		fToplevel->DoSendConfigure();
@@ -76,6 +79,8 @@
 void WaylandWindow::FrameResized(float newWidth, float newHeight)
 {
 	WaylandEnv vlEnv(this);
+	if (fToplevel == NULL)
+		return;
 
 	if (fToplevel->fSizeChanged) {
 		fToplevel->fSizeChanged = false;
